pouch boundary-line patch 0066 - a C11 thread registers its clear_child_tid and tid as a pthread does (thread-model C7).

0004 replaced musl's clone -- which set CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID on
&__thread_list_lock for every new thread -- with SYS_THREAD_SPAWN, and
re-armed that handoff inside start() with SYS_set_tid_address, which also
returns the tid start() stores in self->tid before any __tl_lock (#111).
start_c11(), the thrd_create entry, got neither. __pthread_exit takes the
thread-list lock and leaves it for the kernel to release at exit through
clear_child_tid; a C11 thread had none, so it exited holding the lock, and
thrd_join -- and every later thread create or exit -- waited forever. The
patch's own dossier listed thrd_create as "patched but untested".

  src/thread/pthread_create.c    start_c11() does start()'s registration
      before it restores the mask (0065) and runs the thread's function.

The witness is pouch-hello-threads `mask-c11`, which makes and joins two
thrd_create threads: without this patch the program hangs at the first
join (seen at C7 phase f, 2026-10-29).

--- a/src/thread/pthread_create.c
+++ b/src/thread/pthread_create.c
@@ -249,6 +249,13 @@
 {
 	struct start_args *args = p;
 	int (*start)(void*) = (int(*)(void*)) args->start_func;
+	/* pouch: start()'s registration, which a C11 thread needs as much:
+	 * &__thread_list_lock as clear_child_tid, so SYS_THREAD_EXIT releases
+	 * the thread-list lock __pthread_exit leaves held, and the kernel's tid
+	 * in self->tid before any __tl_lock (#111). */
+	int _pouch_tid = __syscall(SYS_set_tid_address, &__thread_list_lock);
+	if (_pouch_tid < 0) a_crash();
+	__pthread_self()->tid = _pouch_tid;
 	__restore_sigs(&args->sig_mask);
 	__pthread_exit((void *)(uintptr_t)start(args->start_arg));
 	return 0;
